# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hangyul ganada — environment template.
# Copy to .env and fill in. Secrets never belong in source control.
#
# Nothing here is needed to *run* the app. The curriculum, the fonts and every
# pronunciation are bundled with it, and it makes no network request while a
# learner is using it. Everything below configures the content pipeline that
# *builds* those assets, which runs on a developer's machine and not on a phone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Pronunciation build (scripts/content) ---------------------------------

# Which text-to-speech provider generates the bundled audio.
#   edge    Microsoft neural ko-KR voices via the edge-tts client, no credential.
#           This is what the committed assets were generated with.
#   azure   The same voices under a paid Azure Speech subscription. Use this for
#           a commercial release: it is the licence that covers redistributing
#           synthesised audio inside a product.
#   google  Google Cloud Text-to-Speech Neural2 Korean voices.
HANGYUL_TTS_PROVIDER=edge

# Required only for HANGYUL_TTS_PROVIDER=azure.
# AZURE_SPEECH_KEY=
# AZURE_SPEECH_REGION=koreacentral

# Required only for HANGYUL_TTS_PROVIDER=google.
# GOOGLE_TTS_API_KEY=

# --- The build (apps/web) --------------------------------------------------
#
# Where a learner goes when this product has finished teaching them.
#
# Hangyul ganada exists to hand a beginner to the main Hangyul product once they
# can read. The hand-off is built — a card on the alphabet-completion screen and
# a row in My Learning — and it renders *only* when this is set. Unset, both are
# absent from the interface rather than present and leading nowhere.
#
# The value is not in this repository and must not be guessed. What is known:
# the main product is the Expo app `Hangyul` (bundle `com.hangyul.app`, scheme
# `hangyul`), its backend is `api.talkhangyul.com`, and this app is served from
# `ganada.talkhangyul.com`. Neither repository declares a learner-facing web
# address for the main app, so the destination — a landing page, a store
# listing, or a universal link — has to come from whoever owns the product.
#
# Read by `apps/web/src/config/product.ts`; `npm run routing:check` reports
# which way a build went.
# VITE_HANGYUL_URL=

# An address a learner can write to for help. Same rule: unset, nothing in the
# interface offers one.
# VITE_SUPPORT_EMAIL=
